      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "APPENZELL (2) was well supported last time and ran up to expectations, scorching early to score a 1.5 lengths win at Hobart over 461m in 25.79. Ran the fastest time on the program in his latest win. Great chance to get the job done again. CARISSA'S BABY (4) tends to drift back and work into the race, finishing out of the placings two back before charging home into the minors latest when second (26.14) in a Grade 5 at Hobart last time. Has a good record here including five wins. Will give a great sight again. AARIELLA'S GIRL (3) is a capable type and proved too classy last time to win by 2.75 lengths at Hobart in a handy 19.34 beating CARISSA'S BABY. The form from her last run stacks up well. Leading player again. ROMEO INDY (7) is a last-start placegetter who is in the mix again.",
